course: dictionary
lesson: 9338
title: Spiny: built for protection
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Spiny means covered with spines, which are sharp, stiff points like thorns or prickles. You can see the word's parts: spine plus y, so spiny means "full of spines". The comparative forms are spinier and spiniest.
explain: Look at the clues in «A cactus has thick, waxy, spiny stems that store water for the desert.» The stems have sharp points, and the sentence says they store water in a desert. Spines help a plant survive where water is hard to find.
explain: Spines are a kind of protection, called an adaptation. «The echidnas (spiny anteaters of Australia and New Guinea) are mammals that lay eggs.» Their spines keep predators away, so a spiny animal has a defence that a soft animal does not.
explain: Safety first: spiny sea creatures can hurt you. Never touch them on the beach, even when they look interesting. Look, but keep your hands to yourself.
fact: Spiny means covered with spines, which are sharp, stiff points like thorns or prickles.
fact: Spines are a defence: they help stop predators from eating an animal or plant.
fact: Spiny animals include hedgehogs, porcupines, echidnas, sea urchins and spiny lobsters.
fact: Spiny plants include cactuses and holly.
fact: Do not touch spiny sea creatures on the beach.
exercise: «A cactus has thick, waxy, spiny stems that store water for the desert.» What does spiny mean in this sentence? | *Covered with sharp, stiff points | Soft and smooth | Green and shiny | Very wet
exercise: Which of these is a spiny animal? | A duck | *A hedgehog | A goldfish
exercise: «The platypus and the echidnas (spiny anteaters of Australia and New Guinea) are mammals that lay eggs.» Find and copy the word that tells you the echidnas are covered in spines. | *spiny | platypus | mammals | Australia
test: Why do spiny plants like the cactus and holly have spines? | To hold water in the sea | To help them grow taller | To make them smell nice | *To protect themselves from animals that want to eat them
test: Which sentence about spiny sea creatures is correct? | *Do not touch spiny sea creatures on the beach | Spiny lobsters are safe to hold | Hold a sea urchin to take it home | Touch sea urchins to see how they feel
exam: Which is the correct comparative of spiny, meaning more spiny? | spinest | *spinier | spinyer | spinnier
